  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef received an array AAA of NNN integers as a valentine's day present. He wants to **maximize** the length of the **longest strictly increasing subsequence** by choosing a **subarray** and adding a fixed integer XXX to all its elements.\n\nMore formally, Chef wants to **maximize** the length of the longest strictly increasing subsequence of AAA by performing the following operation at most once:\n\n\nPick 333 integers L,RL, RL,R and X&nbsp;(1≤L≤R≤N,&nbsp;X∈Z)X \\ (1 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq N, \\ X \\in \\mathbb{Z})X&nbsp;(1≤L≤R≤N,&nbsp;X∈Z) and assign Ai:=Ai+X&nbsp;∀&nbsp;i∈[L,R]A_i := A_i + X \\ \\forall \\ i \\in [L, R]Ai​:=Ai​+X&nbsp;∀&nbsp;i∈[L,R].\nFind the length of the longest **strictly** increasing sequence Chef can obtain after performing the operation **at most once**.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN, the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers, where the ithi^{th}ith integer denotes AiA_{i}Ai​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the length of the longest **strictly** increasing sequence Chef can obtain.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤2×1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\times 10^51≤N≤2×105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_{i} \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 2 1\n5\n1 5 8 6 9\n4\n1 2 2 1",
        "output": "3\n5\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Chef can pick (L,R,X)=(3,3,2)(L,R,X)=(3,3,2)(L,R,X)=(3,3,2). On performing the operation, AAA becomes [1,2,3][1,2,3][1,2,3]. The LIS of the updated array has length 333. The elements of the LIS are [1,2,3][1,2,3][1,2,3].\nTest case 222: Chef can pick (L,R,X)=(2,3,−3)(L,R,X)=(2,3,-3)(L,R,X)=(2,3,−3). On performing the operation, AAA becomes [1,2,5,6,9][1,2,5,6,9][1,2,5,6,9]. The LIS of the updated array has length 555. The elements of the LIS are [1,2,5,6,9][1,2,5,6,9][1,2,5,6,9].\nTest case 333: Chef can pick (L,R,X)=(4,4,4)(L,R,X)=(4,4,4)(L,R,X)=(4,4,4). On performing the operation, AAA becomes [1,2,2,5][1,2,2,5][1,2,2,5]. The LIS of the updated array has length 333. The elements of the LIS are [1,2,5][1,2,5][1,2,5]."
      }
    ]
  },
